.TH CLONE_MU2E_REPOS.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
clone_mu2e_repos.sh \- clone every repository of the Mu2e GitHub organisation into ./Mu2e/<repo>
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash bin/clone_mu2e_repos.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each line of
.B gh repo list mu2e \-\-limit 4000
runs
.B gh repo clone
.I owner/repo owner/repo
in the current directory, so clones land in
.IR ./Mu2e/<repo> .
An existing target directory makes that one clone fail and the loop
continue.
No shebang; run it with
.BR bash .
.PP
Not control\-room software.
For the DAQ repositories, cloning the
.B mu2edaq\-main
superproject with
.B \-\-recurse\-submodules
gives the pinned set; nothing in the suite clones the whole organisation.
.SH OPTIONS
None; arguments are ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR gh 's
authentication environment
.RB ( GH_TOKEN ,
.BR GH_HOST ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the last
.B gh repo clone
in the pipeline.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
mkdir ~/mu2e\-all && cd ~/mu2e\-all && bash /path/to/bin/clone_mu2e_repos.sh
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR list_issues_mu2e.sh (1),
.BR list_pr_mu2e.sh (1),
.BR gh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
